    "explanation": "A subsystem is a system in its own right, so the same decomposition step applies to it. For example, a computer decomposes into a CPU and memory, and the CPU decomposes further into an arithmetic/logic unit, a control unit, and registers. Repeating the process produces a hierarchy of levels, each more detailed than the one above.",
    "reference": "ch02.pptx (slide 10) · CIS 4100-03_Assignment_2_Juarez.docx (question 2.3) · CIS 4100 Chapters 1-4 Study Guide.md (Chapter 2 — Systems and architecture)"
