    "explanation": "Hardware decomposition breaks a physical system into its smaller physical subsystems. A phone's display, battery, and circuit board assemblies are each subsystems that work together, and each could be decomposed further, for example the circuit board into a processor and memory chips. Splitting the phone into these assemblies is therefore a hardware decomposition.",
    "reference": "ch02.pptx (slide 10–11) · CIS 4100-03_Assignment_2_Juarez.docx (question 2.3) · CIS 4100 Chapters 1-4 Study Guide.md (Chapter 2 — Systems and architecture)"
