    "answer": 1,
    "explanation": "Decomposition stops at the level of detail needed for the question being studied; below that, a component is treated as a single unit, or 'black box'. For example, a network administrator planning capacity treats each server as one component and never needs to decompose it into chips. The misconception is that a complete analysis requires the finest possible detail; the right depth depends on the purpose of the analysis. Decomposition continues only to the level of detail the analysis needs; beyond that, a component is treated as a single unit.",
